From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: opi5 <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rknpu: build and run on mainline 6.18

The source preparation in customize-image-npu.sh, as one diff:
- add rknpu_mem.c (the memory ioctls) and a voltage-aware rknpu_devfreq.c,
  from npu-patches/
- NULL-guard regulator reads in GET_VOLT and debugfs
- copy ioctl results back only for ACTION and SUBMIT
- use rknpu_dev->dev for the DRM_GEM fake_dev
- npu-patches/rknpu-multicore.patch: all three cores, gated on IOMMU
  coverage at probe
- a missing rk-dma-heap-cma heap is not fatal at probe
- DMA_HEAP mode (/dev/rknpu), a forced config header, an rk-dma-heap.h
  stub

One change from it: npu-patches/ ships a copy of devfreq/governor.h as
<linux/devfreq-governor.h>, the 6.19 name of that API, for an out-of-tree
build. In-tree, that header includes the kernel's own
drivers/devfreq/governor.h instead, so the governor structures can't drift
from the kernel's. From 6.19 the kernel's include/linux/devfreq-governor.h
comes first on the include path and this one is unused.

Origin: https://github.com/mack42/OrangePi5Pro 6798f7e8af4e
